    "en":  {
               "headline":  "IonQ hits 52-week low as CFO exit and dilution overshadow record quarter",
               "technical":  "IONQ closed at $20.72 on 20 Nov 2026 (−8.76%), just above the day\u0027s low of $20.51. That low is also the new 52-week low. The trend is clearly down. Price sits far below the EMA 50 ($33.22), EMA 100 ($37.12) and EMA 200 ($40.25), the moving averages that track the short-, medium- and long-term trend. All three are stacked in bearish order (50 \u003c 100 \u003c 200). Momentum agrees. MACD, a trend-momentum gauge, is −3.08, below its signal line at −2.26, with a histogram of −0.82, so selling pressure is still growing rather than fading. RSI 14, a 0–100 momentum gauge where under 30 means oversold, is 29.16, just inside oversold territory. Price closed below the lower Bollinger Band at $21.28. The bands mark a typical ±2 standard-deviation range around the 20-day average of $29.35, so a close below them signals a stretched move. Volume of 29.9M shares was about 1.28× the 20-day average of 23.5M, which confirms the selling. Nearest support is the $20.51 low. First resistance is the lower band near $21.28, then the 20-day midline at $29.35 and the EMA 50 at $33.22.",
               "fundamental":  "On 5 Nov 2026 IonQ reported Q3 revenue of $173.8M (+336% y/y), beating the roughly $141M consensus. It raised 2026 guidance to $505–515M from $450–460M. About $83.5M of revenue came from the newly consolidated SkyWater foundry, while the core IonQ Platform segment grew 127% to $90.3M. Backlog (RPO) more than doubled to $1.2B, and Superion 256 capacity is reported sold out for 2027. Losses remain heavy: an operating loss of $433.1M and an adjusted EBITDA loss of $133.6M. The $564M GAAP profit came from a non-cash warrant gain. Pro forma cash is about $3.7B. In the AI value chain, IonQ is still an early-stage bet on quantum computing rather than a current earner from AI infrastructure. Two milestones support the trapped-ion claim: advancing to DARPA QBI Stage C, the only trapped-ion firm to do so, and NVIDIA\u0027s on-premise Superion 256 deployment.",
               "news":  [
                            "5 Nov 2026: Q3 revenue of $173.8M (+336% y/y) beat estimates, and 2026 guidance was raised to $505–515M. The stock had fallen 10.5% during that day\u0027s broad AI and chip sell-off, then rose about 18% on 6 Nov.",
                            "6 Nov 2026: Cantor Fitzgerald cut its price target to $60 from $70 after the results but kept its positive view.",
                            "3 Nov 2026: IonQ closed its all-stock purchase of zero-trust security firm Elisity for about $1.3B, including up to $150M in earnouts. The deal adds to the share count after a $2.0B offering at $40 that closed on 16 Oct.",
                            "13 Nov 2026: CFO Inder Singh stepped down effective immediately, and no reason was given. CEO Niccolo de Masi is acting finance chief until Commvault CFO Gary Merrill joins on 3 Dec, and the stock fell 6.42% to $28.88.",
                            "13 Nov 2026: A prospectus supplement registered up to 34.58M shares for resale by existing holders. IonQ receives no proceeds, and the filing creates a potential supply overhang.",
                            "16–20 Nov 2026: The quantum sector sell-off continued, with IonQ down about 8% on 16 Nov, 5% on 18 Nov and 8.76% on 20 Nov. From 20 Oct, IonQ lost about 33%, Rigetti 37% and D-Wave 44%."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The chart shows no confirmed bottom. Price is at a fresh 52-week low, below all three EMAs, and MACD is still widening lower. In a downtrend, RSI can stay oversold for weeks. Share supply is a real issue: the $2.0B October offering, the roughly $1.3B all-stock Elisity deal and 34.6M registered resale shares. An unexplained CFO exit eight days after earnings, two large integrations at once and a $433M quarterly operating loss all raise execution risk. Higher bond yields also weigh on speculative growth stocks.",
               "opportunity":  "The business news was stronger than the share price suggests: record revenue, raised guidance, a $1.2B backlog and Superion 256 capacity reported sold out for 2027. DARPA QBI Stage C and NVIDIA\u0027s on-premise Superion 256 order are outside validation of the trapped-ion technology. About $3.7B of pro forma cash gives years of runway. The close below the lower Bollinger Band with RSI under 30 marks a stretched condition. A move back above $21.28 and MACD crossing back above its signal line would be early signs of stabilisation.",
               "risks":  [
                             "Further dilution from the 34.58M-share resale registration and future all-stock deals",
                             "Leadership and governance questions after the sudden, unexplained CFO departure",
                             "Integration risk from absorbing SkyWater and Elisity at the same time, plus heavy operating losses ($433.1M in Q3)",
                             "Revenue mix moving toward foundry and security, which weakens the pure trapped-ion story",
                             "A sector-wide sell-off in speculative AI and quantum stocks while bond yields are high"
